<title>UK: UK agency to prosecute ICI over waste leak.</title>
<headline>UK agency to prosecute ICI over waste leak.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Environment Agency said on Friday it is to prosecute ICI Chemicals &amp; Polymers Ltd after effluent from the company's Runcorn plant flowed into the Weston canal, in north west England, in October.</p>
<p>The Agency, a government body which oversees water quality in the UK, claims the unit of Imperial Chemical Industries Plc failed to maintain equipment and breached discharge limits.</p>
<p>It also believes there was an operational procedure failure leading to the effluent leak, a spokesman for the Environment Agency said.</p>
<p>The agency added that it was setting up a team to review the environmental management systems at the ICI plant.</p>
